{title: Savior, Like a Shepherd Lead Us}
{artist: Dorothy A. Thrupp / William B. Bradbury}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: F}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}
{score: savior-like-a-shepherd-lead-us.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Savior, like a [C]shepherd [F]lead us
Much we [Bb]need Thy [F]tender [C]care
In Thy [F]pleasant [C]pastures [F]feed us
For our [Bb]use Thy [F]folds pre[C]pare
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Blessed Jesus, [Bb]blessed Jesus
[F]Thou hast [C]bought us, [F]Thine we are
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]We are Thine, do [C]Thou be[F]friend us
Be the [Bb]Guardian [F]of our [C]way
Keep Thy [F]flock, from [C]sin de[F]fend us
Seek us [Bb]when we [F]go a[C]stray
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Thou hast promised [C]to re[F]ceive us
Poor and [Bb]sinful [F]though we [C]be
Thou hast [F]mercy [C]to re[F]lieve us
Grace to [Bb]cleanse, and [F]power to [C]free
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Early let us [C]seek Thy [F]favor
Early [Bb]let us [F]do Thy [C]will
Blessed [F]Lord and [C]only [F]Savior
With Thy [Bb]love our [F]bosoms [C]fill
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Refrain}
[F]Blessed Jesus, [Bb]blessed Jesus
[F]Thou hast [C]loved us, [F]love us still
{end_of_verse}
